<title>BELGIUM: EU experts to consider intervention quality test.</title>
<headline>EU experts to consider intervention quality test.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's cereals management committee will discuss on Thursday a proposal to introduce quality tests for wheat sold into intervention, an EU official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;In view of the effects of the weather on this year's crop the committee will discuss the introduction of germinative tests to ensure wheat is of bread making quality when sold into intervention,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The possibility of germinative tests was introduced five years ago and can be introduced on an annual basis. --Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
